CONCEPT A white polar research station. The landmark is a tall round core tower (r 8, four floors plus a dome and antenna spire) wrapped by a low ring of labs with an orange stripe on its accent floor. A wide glass lab wing attaches to the east, and a low hangar-like machine hall plugs into the south with a landing pad on its roof. Materials: white concrete on pillar and wall2, smooth quartz base, orange 
