CRITIQUE r1 claude-sonnet-5-5: 5 flaws in 15s, ~$0.0426
  flaw: Balcony on the core's north side was skipped (no spot). The ring hugs the core, so the core wall is hidden up to the ring height and the balcony level fell on a covered wall.
    fix: Moved the balcony to the core's top-floor level 4 (above the ring) and set the side to s. The core's south wall is exposed above the ring there.
  flaw: The core dome is solid orange and reads as a pumpkin/orange cap rather than a white station with an orange stripe. The orange trim role on the core makes it dominant.
    fix: Removed the core's orange trim override so the trim stays light gray. The orange now appears only as the accent stripe.
  flaw: The landing pad sits on the hangar roof but the hangar's flat roof reads small and the pad is hidden behind the ring. The pad should be more visible on a wide roof.
    fix: Widened the hangar from 21 to 23 so the pad roof has more room; the machine hall footprint was only enlarged.
  flaw: The platform feature on the core with side top is meaningless: platform is a terraced base under the whole site and it was attached to the core's top.
    fix: Kept the platform but moved it to the ring (on labs) with size 1 so it reads as a site base.
  flaw: The glass labs wing is a single band-window box with little depth; the facade is plain.
    fix: Added a porch on glass_labs' west side... replaced by a blade_sign on glass_labs' east side so the glow accent reads.
